In the automotive industry, closed-loop processes are not popular. Other parts like car mechanics, dismantlers, demolishers or dealers fulfil a crucial function in the reuse of products through the second-hand market, reuse of parts, material recycling and prolonging life by maintenance and repair. The existing recovery system, market and regulation play a big role in determining the lifecycle scenarios of automobiles. However, this system does not come with a version that is integrated with other car services. In order to create an efficient closed-loop supply chain, it is essential to create collaboration and dialogue between the different stakeholders involved.